<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tatya Tope</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a>–<a href="/years/1859">1859</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Tantia Tope, Ramachandra Pandurang Tope</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tatya Tope was one of the leading commanders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-rebellion-of-1857">Indian Rebellion of 1857</a>. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanaya">Nana</a> Sahib, he fought at Kanpur, joined forces with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshmibai">Rani Lakshmibai</a> of Jhansi and took Gwalior in 1858, then led British columns on a long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> chase across central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Betrayed in 1859, he was tried and hanged at Shivpuri.</p></div>
